AWS EBS(elastic block store)

it is cloud based storage service that provides durable , high performance block storage for ec2 instance
its like virtual hard drive that allows you to store and access data even the ec2 instance is stopped or terminated

it is region and avalability zone specific
it can used for snapshot for backup 


EBS snapshot
if we want to copy our data to new az or new region

copy ebs from one az to other

click on created volume of ebs -> click on action -> click on create snapshot
then click on snapshot from ebs -> click on action -> click on create volume from snapshot -> select az -> create volume

then create new instance in the new az -> t oadd az go to networking and and in subnet select az -> go to volumes and attach volume of az 

copy snapshot from one region to other 
select volume -> click on action -> click on copy snapshot -> select region where want to copy


amazon data life cycle manager provide simple and automated way to backup data store in EBS volume

go to life cycle manager in volumes 
here we can use default policy or custome policy 

for custom policy
1st add tag for the volume like key and value by clicking the volume and go to manage tag

the got to custom policy of life cycle manager there add that key and value in target resource by selecting volume 
give policy description as you want  then next 
in schedule then select frequency as you want like daily 
then in advanced setting enable what you want like cross region copy if you want



